    "body": "Summary\nThere is currently no Windows client for bitchat. This limits adoption for users who rely on Windows as their primary desktop OS and want to participate in the mesh network without needing an Apple device.\nCurrent state\nBitchat is available on iOS and macOS. The codebase appears to be Swift-based, which ties it tightly to Apple platforms.\nRequest\nAdd a Windows-compatible client, either as:\n\nA native port using a cross-platform language (e.g. Rust, Go, or Flutter), or\nA standalone Windows application that implements the same Bluetooth LE mesh protocol\n\nWhy this matters\n\nWindows holds the majority desktop market share globally\nUsers without Apple hardware are fully excluded from the network, which weakens the mesh\nA cross-platform implementation would also make future Linux support more feasible\n\nNotes\n\nWindows has Bluetooth LE support via the Windows.Devices.Bluetooth API (available from Windows 10 v1703+)\nA protocol spec or documentation of the mesh layer would help third-party contributors attempt a Windows client independently\nHappy to help test on Windows 10/11 if development starts",
